<Project>
  <!--
    T01 (docs/build-orchestration-plan.md, "Build scaffolding and CI"): centralised settings for
    IC2.sln's *new* projects only.

    This file deliberately applies NOTHING to the pre-existing projects (src/IC2.Data,
    src/IC2.Inspect) or to godot/IC2.MapViewer.csproj: none of them are named in the condition
    below, so each keeps exactly the TargetFramework/Nullable/ImplicitUsings it already declares in
    its own .csproj, and none of them opt in to TreatWarningsAsErrors. This is intentional per the
    T01 task entry ("existing IC2.Data/IC2.Inspect opt out, to avoid a scaffolding task turning into
    a refactor") and its hazard note (do not "fix" existing IC2.Data/IC2.Inspect code).

    godot/IC2.MapViewer.csproj is additionally EXCLUDED FROM IC2.sln entirely (see IC2.sln itself):
    it requires the Godot 4.7.2 .NET SDK, which is not installed on CI runners, so it cannot build
    there. That exclusion is independent of this file and would apply even if this condition matched
    it (it does not — "IC2.MapViewer" is not in the list below).

    New projects the backlog will need (src/IC2.Engine, src/IC2.Cli, tests/IC2.Engine.Tests,
    tests/IC2.Data.Tests) are pre-declared here by T01 and opt in to the strict settings by project
    name below, so that centralising them in one file does not require editing each new .csproj by
    hand every time a later task adds files to one of these projects.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="
      '$(MSBuildProjectName)' == 'IC2.Engine' OR
      '$(MSBuildProjectName)' == 'IC2.Cli' OR
      '$(MSBuildProjectName)' == 'IC2.Engine.Tests' OR
      '$(MSBuildProjectName)' == 'IC2.Data.Tests'">
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
